cb933a-628f-4003-9966-edf0cc086d3e" class="r-ihhr73 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>1 in 5</p></span></div><div data-rid="69b5af56-be33-4a5c-b596-5a2f18ddec8c" class="r-1bni5fb alchemy-rte" style="--replo-library-c1a8c56f-d134-48db-bdea-c4ba0a1e6710-styles-4e9e1fb4-94ca-474b-82ac-38d78f5aef1d-attributes-color:#ffffff"><span style="width:100%"><p>CRAMPS are FROM low electrolytes</p></span></div><div data-rid="d066b544-d93c-4686-97db-fe6cfb1326c4" class="r-lsvdnc alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>potassium plays a direct role in muscle contraction and nerve signaling, and inadequate electrolyte balance is commonly associated with cramping and fatigue.</p></span></div><a data-rid="5f036a52-fdc3-450b-beeb-88c5e11ef9d0" tabindex="0" role="link" class="r-1fk2e9c alchemy-rte" target="_blank" href="https://nap.nationalacademies.org/read/25353/chapter/13" rel="noreferrer"><p>SOURCE: schwellnus et al., british journal of sports medicine</p></a></div><div data-rid="8dcbc70d-0b5c-40cf-b550-36093bdbaf78" class="r-15c05pl"><div class="r-i3pb33" data-rid="1"><div data-rid="138b8259-9e90-48d5-8afa-33b46f5f0102" class="r-6jr9ur"><div data-rid="5fb4f47c-d510-489f-b804-6a4adc944143" class="r-hd3rhx"><div data-rid="3334e410-6e0a-4afd-8d4c-984b1b790bc3" class="r-15x9urz"><div data-rid="96a7917d-e2a4-4d60-bf19-b0146e3e4537" class="r-ispxl"><div data-rid="b15a7381-427f-424d-ae37-5dc39a217785" class="r-nf8mhp alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>serving: 180 milligrams</p></span></div></div><div data-rid="b233aabb-aaad-447c-8a1b-3c2bd3c43170" class="r-nlsb00"><div data-rid="f6f2cbf1-c319-42a0-9f77-b7be0d2c8a98" class="r-iphtaf alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>MUSCLE CONTRACTION</p></span></div><div data-rid="eea06635-5442-49d8-9181-2f9749b3fda1" class="r-1sn0zcv alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>NERVE SIGNALING</p></span></div><div data-rid="e8421660-2c31-41f4-9bb2-2af3cba1d8f0" class="r-1ew24lg alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>ELECTROLYTE SUPPORT</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="8c6970a6-f0b0-476c-9a3f-0553af92f333" class="r-19cxo14 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>SLIDE 9 OF 10</p></span></div></div></div></div></div><div data-replo-component-root="carousel" data-replo-part="slide" data-replo-root-id="replo-carousel:R2uhj2:" data-slide-index="9" data-slide-source-index="9" data-is-cloned="true" data-slide-id="replo-carousel:R2uhj2::slide:9:9" id="replo-carousel:R2uhj2::slide:9:9:R2muhj2::clone:9" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" role="group" aria-label="Slide 10" style="display:flex;height:100%;padding:0;margin:0;backface-visibility:hidden;flex-shrink:0;position:relative" data-component-id="dfac2b96-a4e5-4b62-9a7b-4351248d42bc" class="r-1pcf6i6"><div data-rid="dfac2b96-a4e5-4b62-9a7b-4351248d42bc" class="r-yfwa95"><div data-rid="2452a37c-783b-4598-a623-693a9d6fe5ff" class="r-15tzzc"></div><div data-rid="923a4cb6-c44b-4eba-b87a-1298e37819ee" class="r-rlrspq"><div data-rid="54664bd7-468e-47ca-903a-d159eaad5603" class="r-oj5znx"><div data-rid="f8f0be98-62af-4a05-b46b-d91d5e3ed8f6" class="r-v1et8b alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>SODIUM CITRATE</p></span></div><div data-rid="5dc7f6bf-432f-46d6-b497-e591f9b11856" class="r-qefpuc alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>+2.9%</p></span></div><div data-rid="3f290464-bc36-4916-80df-c5a1fb3dbd9f" class="r-1n4fqli alchemy-rte" style="--replo-library-c1a8c56f-d134-48db-bdea-c4ba0a1e6710-styles-4e9e1fb4-94ca-474b-82ac-38d78f5aef1d-attributes-color:#ffffff"><span style="width:100%"><p>AVERAGE PERFORMANCE IMPROVEMENT</p></span></div><div data-rid="c36e29c8-e961-4d9f-ae82-25dab66a1f68" class="r-1hp4spy alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>IN A DOUBLE-BLIND, PLACEBO-CONTROLLED CROSSOVER STUDY, SODIUM CITRATE IMPROVED PERFORMANCE ACROSS MULTIPLE MAX-EFFORT FITNESS TESTS WITH AN AVERAGE +2.9% IMPROVEMENT (AND UP TO&nbsp;~4-5% ON CERTAIN MOVEMENTS).</p></span></div><a data-rid="e7645991-f482-4b58-9cf0-1c4e53b61177" tabindex="0"